The Board of Directors of the Toronto Atmospheric Fund:

1. Approved the allocation of $946,000 to support Toronto Atmospheric Fund programs in 2024 as outlined below, to be funded from the Canada, Ontario, and Toronto endowments except where otherwise indicated:

a. Accelerate deployment of electric vehicles (EV) and charging: $14,000 to expand EV charging for multi-family building residents and vehicle for hire drivers;

b. Decarbonizing Ontario’s electricity system: $94,000 support the region’s transition to a net-zero grid;

c. Retrofit Accelerator: $265,000 to build the market for deep retrofits by collaborating with leading building operators and industry solutions providers to deliver deeper retrofits faster and more cost-effectively;

d. Impact Investing: $100,000 to support investments in impact-first projects/companies, maintain management and compliance of the Toronto Atmospheric Fund’s investment portfolio, and enable prudent investment of at least $5 million;

e. Climate Policy: $50,000 (from Canada and Toronto endowments only) to be an effective and influential advocate for urban climate policy with all three levels of government;

f. Research and Innovation: $95,000 to deliver critical internal and community capacity needed to support effective design and delivery of Toronto Atmospheric Fund-funded initiatives;

g. Communications and Campaigns: $36,000 to increase Toronto Atmospheric Funds’s overall audience reach while maintaining our high engagement levels towards all focus area priorities;

h. Grants: $52,600 to build the internal and community capacity needed to support effective design and delivery of Toronto Atmospheric Fund-funded initiatives;

